# **Level 25's item slot 1 object, collected and spent** — the `$0A` at
# (128,694) that `zamn_assets route` refused for a dozen rounds, walked to in
# the emulator rather than in the tool.
#
# **It is not what took `psn_t3_expired`.** That was `movies/level29-item.zmv`,
# in the round that corrected the search's box; this fires it a second time, at
# frame 4551, and reaches 208 of the 538 branch sites on its own. Whether any of
# those 208 is new to the corpus is a question for `verify_corpus.ps1`, not for
# this header. What it is for is the other claim. Two rounds of route work
# ended with `route`
# printing a walk to (127,700) and calling this object reachable, and that was
# the search's own terrain test agreeing with itself. This is the game agreeing.
#
# **The prefix is `movies/level25-boss.zmv` through frame 2872**, where the
# player stands at (1017,644), off the escalator and before that movie's
# north-plaza detour. The escalator is why nothing can start at the spawn:
# `tools/fit_route.py` plans a leg, releases, and measures itself back where it
# began, because an escalator moves the player while the button is up. From
# 2872 the route is **184 cells in 11 legs and 732 frames**, against the
# 231 cells in 12 legs and 921 frames the spawn costs.
#
# **The fitter still could not walk it.** Sixty legs, the last forty of them
# 8-frame unstick nudges that moved nothing, stopped at (119,696) — nine pixels
# short. The reason is worth the movie on its own:
#
# **A direction change does not take effect on the frame it is pressed.** The
# player finishes the step he is already in, and where that lands him decides
# whether the new leg is walkable at all. Standing at (119,696) and pressing
# Right puts him at (119,694) and then nowhere for 100 frames, because
# `$80:AE14` calls (121,694) **blocked** — col 16, row 85, tile `$0E9`,
# attribute `$0003`, the wall this object is tucked under. Walking *down*
# through (111,696) and turning Right on that frame carries him to y=702
# instead, and the same eastward leg is clear for forty pixels. Same button,
# same pixel, two lanes, and only one of them is a route. `zamn_assets probe
# 26 119 694` and `probe 26 121 694` are the two commands that say so.
#
# So the last two legs are tuned by hand and the tuning is one frame wide:
# `Right` at 3632, while the Down leg is still running, then `Up` at 3640, which
# stops against that same wall at **(127,696)** — one and two pixels from the
# object, inside `actor_overlap_pass`'s box on both axes.
#
# The tail, from `--watch`:
#
#     3643  $1D0E 0 -> 1                 he walks onto the object
#     3682  $1CC0 7 -> 1                 A cycles the selection onto it
#     3702  $54 = $8000, $56 = 849, with $1D0E back to 0 and $1CC0 back to 7:
#           X spends it, the slot empties, and the selection moves off
#     4551  $56 -> 0 and $54 -> 0 in the same frame — the branch
#
# 849 frames of countdown and not one of them interrupted, spent standing where
# the walk ended.
#
# `zamn_cosim verify -f 4600` checks 270,527 calls with nothing diverged.

